course: dictionary
lesson: 2133
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Cool is one of them. You can find its meaning by reading the words around it. «A cool breeze blew across the beach» tells you cool means a little cold, pleasantly not warm, because a breeze is air moving outside.
explain: Cool can also mean calm. If someone says «Stay cool» during a fright, they mean keep calm and do not get upset. Cool can even mean great, as in «That's cool!», which is slang. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence?
explain: Cool can be a verb too. In «Let the cake cool», cool means to become colder. Science uses this idea: hot things lose heat until they match the room, and sweating cools your body.
fact: Cool is a word with many meanings, so always check the sentence around it.
fact: Cool can mean a little cold, calm, great (slang), or not friendly.
fact: As a verb, cool means to make or become colder: «Let hot food cool before eating.»
fact: «Cool» in the phrase «keep your cool» means stay calm and not get upset.
fact: «Cool» can also describe a reply that is not friendly, as in «a cool reply».
exercise: «A cool breeze blew across the beach.» What does cool mean here? | Fashionable and great | Very angry | Quick and loud | *A little cold, pleasantly not warm
exercise: Mum says, «Stay cool, we can fix this.» What does cool mean here? | Freezing cold, like ice | Very loud | *Calm, not upset | Wet with rain
exercise: Find the word in «Let the cake cool before you eat it» that means to become colder. | Let | *cool | cake | before
test: «Her reply was cool, and she did not smile.» What does cool mean here? | Great and fashionable | Calm after a fright | *Not friendly | Very cold to touch
test: Why does chocolate stay hard on a «cool shelf»? | Because the shelf is in the sun | Because chocolate likes shelves | *Because the shelf is cooler than your body, so the chocolate does not melt | Because the shelf is wet
exam: Someone says, «Keep your cool, Sam.» What does keep your cool mean? | Wear a warm jumper | Keep the fridge running | *Stay calm and do not get upset | Run as fast as you can
